    "type": "toggle",
    "label": "Show 90° lone-pair–bond-pair repulsions",
    "default": false,
    "teaches": "Counting the 90° lone-pair–bond-pair contacts (4 for panel b, 6 for panel c, 5 for panel d) explains quantitatively why equatorial lone pairs are preferred and why panel (b) is the real geometry of ClF3."
