]

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "heightFraction": 0.6
}

NOTES: Build each bipyramid as a reusable Group: LineSegments (or thick Line2) for the 10 outer edges with the single rear equatorial edge as a LineDashedMaterial (call computeLineDistances), a ShapeGeometry/MeshBasicMaterial triangle with transparent:true, depthWrite:false, side:DoubleSide for the shaded equatorial plane, and per-vertex bond cylinders/lines whose material swaps between gray and red based on the current panel state. Labels (Cl, F, Equatorial, Axial, panel captions) as CSS2DObject or sprite text so they stay screen-facing and legible while orbiting. Panel switching should crossfade or just rebuild bond colors on the same shared frame so the learner sees only the lone pairs move. Highlight mode from the click interaction: emissive/thicker outline plus a soft colored halo on the two axial or three equatorial vertices in every visible structure simultaneously. Repulsion overlay: thin translucent arcs (TorusGeometry segments or line arcs) between each lone pair and each 90°-adjacent bond, with a count badge. Default camera is a standard isometric pose, slight tilt above the equatorial plane so the plane reads as an ellipse; orbit limited in polar angle to keep the vertical axis upright. Flat white background, no shadows, no specular — match the line-art look of the textbook.

